// W4e surface fold-in — shell parameter expansion (parse-only fixture).
//
// GRADUATION: the shell DSL's parameter expansion enters the PBG grammar now
// (wyrd-83wx) — the simple form `$name` (the committed `variable_expansion`)
// beside the braced form `${name}`, folded into `variable_expansion` as a
// second opener branch. The braced form is a W4e divergence from the committed
// tree-sitter grammar (which has only `$name`); its interior is a shell
// `variable_name`, DISTINCT from the string-interpolation `${ E }` host-splice
// (a shell parameter is not a gandr binding). The SEMANTICS — the gandr-shell
// host seam answering an expansion against the process environment — graduate
// under the wyrd-83wx gandr-shell wiring follow-up. Parse-only; never lowered.

// A single-quoted string is a verbatim literal run: `$x` and backslashes inside
// it are NOT expanded or escaped (grammar.js `single_quoted_string`).
#!{ printf 'literal $x and \n stay verbatim'; }

// `$name` simple expansion beside `${name}` braced expansion.
#!{ echo $HOME ${HOME}; }

// The braced form disambiguates a parameter from adjacent word text — `${x}`
// abuts a following word, and two braced parameters abut with no separator.
#!{ echo ${prefix}_suffix ${x}${y}; }
